      "name": "Saturating lane",
      "module_name": "release_saturating_lane",
      "parent_id": null,
      "behavior": "One scalar elastic output-slot lane. data_i packs signed 4-bit a in high nibble and b in low nibble. Compute a+b with enough intermediate width; clamp to[-8,7]; encode result in unsigned4-bit two's-complement data_o. Reset data_o=0,valid_o=0. can_accept=(!old_valid_o)||ready_i; if can_accept then valid_o=valid_i and update data_o only for valid input; else hold. ready_o=(!new_valid_o)||ready_i after edge.  Sample active-low rst_array_n synchronously only on rising clk_array edges; no asynchronous reset response.",
      "test_expectations": "Preserve all independent16-cycle scalar expectations, including signed positive and negative saturation, stalls, idle data retention and reset flush. Four instances must later be checked with the independent24-cycle system contract.",
